    "perplexity": {
      "description": "Released in 1995 on A&M Records, Dopes to Infinity is the third studio album by Monster Magnet and the record that pushed the band further into the cosmic, riff-heavy sound that made them a major force in 1990s hard rock. Built on thick guitars, swaggering grooves, and a hazy psychedelic edge, the album balances raw aggression with a larger, space-rock sense of atmosphere.\n\nIts best-known track, “Negasonic Teenage Warhead,” became the band’s first hit single and helped bring Monster Magnet wider attention. The album was recorded in New York and is often remembered as one of the defining statements of stoner rock, combining heavy-metal weight, retro rock attitude, and a memorable melodic hook sense that earned it strong cult status and favorable critical notice.",
